3, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01KBVLK1vr1oLqVXb9ncAoU8", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_timeout"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 410003, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KBVLK1vr1oLqVXb9ncAoU8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 414008, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 \u2014 https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the docstring.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BskAbch9mAPuaHGQi4Tgcu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KWgNiwMMyJAVJaZhMZpKFQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SDNi1i9tzqETXEQNeRWk28", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use",