: "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 \u2014 https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the docstring.", "type": "text"}]}]}